## PART 3 — UNIFIED WORK ORDER ARCHITECTURE

### 3.1 Target Operational Entity Hierarchy

```
Season (موسم)
  └── Field / Pivot (بيفوت)  ← maps 1:1 to cost_center
        └── Work Order (أمر عمل)
              ├── operation_type: SRV_MECH | SRV_LABOR | SRV_IRRIG | SRV_CHEM | SRV_HARVEST
              ├── Work Tasks (مهام عمالة)   ← quantity × unit_cost → labor cost
              ├── Equipment Lines (معدات)    ← hours × cost/h → equipment cost → immediate GL
              └── Inventory Issues (صرف)     ← item × qty × cost → inventory cost → GL via outbox
```

### 3.2 Unified Lifecycle Per Work Order

```
STEP 1: Create Work Order
  POST /api/operations/orders
  Required: name, operation_type, planned_date, season_id, field_id
  Auto-derive: center_code ← fields.center_code
  Status: pending

STEP 2: Execute — Add Tasks / Equipment / Inventory Issues
  POST /api/operations/orders/:id/tasks         → work_tasks (no immediate GL)
  POST /api/operations/orders/:id/equipment     → work_order_equipment + immediate GL
  POST /api/inventory/movements/batch (ISSUE)   → inventory_movements + GL via outbox
    Payload MUST include: work_order_id, center_code (inherited), field_id (inherited)
  Status: in_progress

STEP 3: Complete
  PATCH /api/operations/orders/:id/status → done

STEP 4: Cost & Close
  PATCH /api/operations/orders/:id/status → costed
  TRIGGERS: resolveWorkOrderLabor() for all unposted work_tasks + unposted equipment
  Status: costed (terminal — immutable)

STEP 5: Supplier Invoice Matching (optional, for externally supplied services)
  POST /api/suppliers/:code/transactions (entry_type=د)
    Payload MUST include: work_order_id (links invoice to WO)
  This does NOT double-post: supplier invoice posts AP/Expense GL.
  Work order tasks/equipment already posted the operational cost GL.
  → These are DIFFERENT GL entries: one for accrual, one for payable recognition.
```

### 3.3 Duplicate Prevention Rules

| Scenario | Prevention |
|----------|-----------|
| Equipment posted via WO + also via supplier invoice | Work Order equipment GL = operational cost (DR WIP/Expense / CR Accrued Liabilities). Supplier invoice GL = AP recognition (DR Accrued Liabilities / CR AP). Net = zero double-posting. |
| Labor posted via work_tasks + also via supplier invoice | Only one path allowed per WO. If SRV_LABOR supplier invoice exists, do NOT add work_tasks for same labor. |
| Inventory already issued (ISSUE movement) + WO costed | Work_tasks cost does NOT include inventory. `inventory_cost` on WO is read from `inventory_movements.value_out WHERE work_order_id = ?` — never double-posted. |

### 3.4 Current Gap vs. Target — What Needs to Change

| Gap | Fix Required |
|-----|-------------|
| All 700 inventory ISSUE movements have no `work_order_id` | Backfill where possible; enforce FK going forward |
| 203 supplier invoices (SRV_MECH + SRV_LABOR) have no `work_order_id` | Create WOs retroactively for historical data OR accept as pre-WO era legacy |
| `supplier_transactions.work_order_id` column exists but is always NULL | Activate: enforce `work_order_id` required for SRV_MECH invoices going forward |
| Work Order module UI exists but is unused | Training + process rollout |

