### 4.3 Cost Propagation Flow

```
Source Transaction
  │
  ├── season_id     → Season P&L reporting
  ├── center_code   → Cost Center reporting (pivot-level)
  ├── field_id      → Field/Pivot profitability
  └── work_order_id → Operation-level cost drill-down

journal_entry_lines
  ├── center_code   → propagated from source via postFromBusinessEvent()
  ├── season_id     → propagated from source via postFromBusinessEvent()
  └── field_id      → propagated from source via postFromBusinessEvent()
```

> **Rule:** `postFromBusinessEvent()` already accepts and propagates all four dimensions. The data model is correct. The enforcement gap is at the API input layer.

### 4.4 Pivot-Level Profitability Model

```
Pivot P&L (per field/pivot per season):

REVENUE:
  + harvest_records.total_revenue (when harvest is recorded)
  + sales_contracts linked to field

DIRECT COSTS:
  + SUM(inventory_movements.value_out) WHERE field_id = pivot
  + SUM(supplier_transactions.amount)  WHERE center_code = pivot_center
  + SUM(work_tasks.quantity * unit_cost) WHERE work_order.field_id = pivot
  + SUM(work_order_equipment.total_cost) WHERE work_order.field_id = pivot

ALLOCATED ADMIN COSTS:
  + center_code = 1006011 (admin) costs allocated by area proportion:
    pivot_area_feddan / total_area_feddan × total_admin_cost

GROSS MARGIN = REVENUE − DIRECT COSTS − ALLOCATED ADMIN
MARGIN PER FEDDAN = GROSS MARGIN / pivot_area_feddan
```

